    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Located on the scenic Doorin Peninsula is this traditional, stone-built cottage. Just over 2km from Mountcharles Village and within 8km of Donegal Town. Occupying an elevated site, set back from the public road creates a peaceful, private and appealing setting. A rear extension was added in the past. Internal accommodation comprises of living room, kitchen, three bedrooms and a bathroom. Vacant for many years, this property requires a major renovation. Subject to meeting the criteria, this property should qualify for various home improvement grants such as the Derelict Home Grant plus the S.E.A.I. Energy Efficiency Upgrade Grants. All enquiries are welcome."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "<br><br>\nLiving Room - 4m x 3.5m <br>Solid fuel range (not working). \nFront facing window. <br><br><br>\nKitchen - 2.7m x 2.7m <br>Stainless steel sink.\nRear facing window. <br><br><br>\nSitting Room / Bedroom One - 4m x 3.8m <br>Open fire. \nDual aspect windows.<br><br><br>\nBedroom Two - 4m x 2.3m <br>Front facing window. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Three - 3.2m x 2.2m <br>Rear facing window. <br><br><br>\nBathroom - 2.3m x 1.4m <br><br><br>"
